  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Prednisolone may be associated with Erythema Multiforme through a chain of indications involving corticosteroids. Specifically, Prednisolone is linked to Chronic Beryllium Disease, which in turn is associated with Methylprednisolone, and both are linked to Erythema Multiforme. Similarly, Prednisolone is connected to Lipoid Nephrosis, which is associated with Hydrocortisone Acetate, which also links to Erythema Multiforme. These pathways highlight a potential role of corticosteroids in the development of Erythema Multiforme, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of support for this relationship, but the evidence is not definitive. The integration of these pathways suggests that corticosteroids may contribute to the pathogenesis of Erythema Multiforme, though further research is needed to establish a causal link.",
